$ gragas check --help
--- stdout

  Reads every file under rulebook/ and checks it: each
  against its JSON Schema, then across files (ids used
  once and kept in ids.lock, a retired rule's
  replacement, each source, kind, facet, binding and
  tool a rule names, folders that are parts), then each
  count against its baseline in baseline.json, which may
  only fall, then, when gate/exemptions.yaml is there,
  each exception row in it (an expired row, a row for a
  rule that is not active, an id listed twice and an
  exit file that is not there fail), and, when
  GRAGAS_NAMES_FILE is set, for names public text
  must not hold. It writes nothing.

    gragas check
    gragas check -C ../gragas
    gragas check --json

  In a folder that holds one rulebook.yaml it checks the
  rulebook instead: validate's findings, then its history
  against the merge base of HEAD and the base ref (the
  base-ref setting, or GRAGAS_BASE_REF): no line of the
  merge base rewritten, no broken link or gap, each commit
  since held to its own entries as guard staged holds one,
  no pin or governance changed without its entry, and no
  rule on trial past the merge base's window. Where the
  merge
  base holds one rulebook, a branch that removes it or adds
  a
  second is a finding. With no base ref it is not ready.

  Below a .gragas/pin.yaml, in the repository the pin lies
  in, it checks the project: its tool configs held to the
  bindings of the rulebook the pin names, its tier contract
  and its exemptions. It ends done with the findings listed;
  --fail-on names the kinds of finding that end it on
  findings. A tool with bindings that could not be asked
  ends it not ready.

  USAGE


    gragas check [--flags]


  FLAGS

    --accessible  Plain questions (ACCESSIBLE)
    --config      The settings file (GRAGAS_CONFIG)
    -C --dir      The repository holding rulebook/ (.)
    --fail-on     End on findings when one is of this kind,
                  below a pin (the kinds are tool-config,
                  tier-contract, exemption, names,
                  tracked-files, counts)
    -h --help     Help for check
    --json        Answer in one JSON document
    --no-color    No colour (NO_COLOR)
    --plain       Print plainly: nothing moves

--- stderr
--- exit 0
